es/Projects/120640/Project%20Image/1_1726052452-thumb.webp)\n\nRegent Jeevan Tara\n\n₹ 1.5 Cr - 3.7 Cr\n\n![Vira Avenue](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/121850/Project%20Image/02-1730117332-thumb.webp)\n\nVira Avenue\n\n₹ 3.65 Cr - 9.5 Cr\n\n![Vira Perfect Parla](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/121703/Project%20Image/02-1729339750-thumb.webp)\n\nVira Perfect Parla\n\n₹ 3.3 Cr - 5.3 Cr\n\n![Goyal Atlantis](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/125328/Project%20Image/Hou-1737957724-thumb.webp)\n\nGoyal Atlantis\n\n₹ 1.9 Cr - 3.8 Cr\n\n![Zee Sai Chintan](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/132144/Project%20Image/1-1765187123-thumb.webp)\n\nZee Sai Chintan\n\n₹ 2.35 Cr - 5.6 Cr\n\n![JRT Arave](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/152982/Project%20Image/khk-1769605509-thumb.webp)\n\nJRT Arave\n\n₹ 90 Lakh - 2.45 Cr\n\n![Kamla Arunkamal](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/149923/Project%20Image/2-1759909999-thumb.webp)\n\nKamla Arunkamal\n\n₹ 1.7 Cr - 4.4 Cr\n\n![Nirmaan Heena](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/155193/Project_Image/3-1774098226.webp)\n\nNirmaan Heena\n\n₹ 2.1 Cr - 4.2 Cr\n\n![Moss Om Gurukrupa SRA CHS](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/155201/Project_Image/1-1774098034.webp)\n\nMoss Om Gurukrupa SRA CHS\n\n₹ 1.25 Cr - 2.2 Cr\n\n![Lakshmi Solitaire](https://imgcdn.houssed.com/assets/Files/Projects/155306/Project_Image/1-1774096839.webp)\n\nLakshmi Solitaire\n\n₹ 2.1 Cr - 3.15 Cr\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What are new projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nNew projects in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** refer to residential developments that are either under construction or recently launched and have future possession timelines. These include apartment projects in early construction stages, mid-stage developments, and near-completion projects that have not yet received an occupancy certificate. Buyers typically consider new projects for phased payment options, modern layouts, updated construction standards, and potential long-term price appreciation within the locality\n\n### How are new project flats in Malabar Hill, Mumbai different from ready-to-move flats?\n\nNew project flats in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** are purchased during the construction phase and offer possession at a future date, while ready-to-move flats are completed and available for immediate occupancy. New projects usually come with lower entry prices and flexible payment schedules but involve waiting periods and construction risk. Ready-to-move flats cost more upfront but provide certainty around possession, condition, and legal completion.\n\n### Are under-construction flats in Malabar Hill, Mumbai cheaper than ready-to-move flats?\n\nIn most cases, **under-construction flats in Malabar Hill, Mumbai** are priced lower than ready-to-move flats in the same neighbourhood. Developers often offer early-stage pricing to attract buyers and support project cash flow. However, buyers should factor in GST, possible price escalations over the construction period, and the time value of money when comparing overall costs.\n\n### What risks should I consider before buying a new project flat in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nKey risks include construction delays, changes in project specifications, financial instability of the developer, and delays in regulatory approvals. Buyers should mitigate these risks by verifying RERA registration, reviewing the developer’s past delivery history, monitoring construction progress, and avoiding projects with unclear land ownership or pending approvals.\n\n### How can I verify whether a new project in Malabar Hill, Mumbai is RERA approved?\n\nEvery RERA-registered project in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** has a unique registration number issued by the state real estate authority. Buyers can verify this number on the official RERA portal to check project approvals, sanctioned plans, committed possession dates, and promoter details. On Houssed, RERA status is clearly highlighted for verified new projects to simplify this verification.\n\n### What possession timelines should I realistically expect for new projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nPossession timelines depend on the construction stage of the project. Early-stage projects may take 3–4 years, mid-stage developments usually require 1–2 years, while near-completion projects may offer possession within 6–12 months. Buyers should rely on the possession date declared under RERA and avoid making decisions based solely on verbal assurances.\n\n### Is GST applicable on new project flats in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nYes, GST is applicable on **under-construction flats in Malabar Hill, Mumbai** as per prevailing tax regulations. GST is not charged on ready-to-move flats that have already received an occupancy certificate. Buyers should confirm whether the quoted price includes GST and understand how it affects the total purchase cost.\n\n### Can I get a home loan for a new project flat in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nMost banks and housing finance companies offer home loans for **RERA-approved new projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai**. Loan disbursement is typically linked to construction milestones, meaning funds are released in stages rather than as a lump sum. Buyers should ensure the project is approved by major lenders and understand the EMI structure during the construction period.\n\n### Are new projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai a good option for investment?\n\nNew projects in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** can be suitable for investment if the locality has strong infrastructure development, rental demand, and long-term growth prospects. Investment returns depend on timely project completion, rental absorption after possession, and overall market conditions. Investors should focus on reputed developers and avoid over-leveraging during the construction phase.\n\n### What documents should I verify before buying a flat in a new project in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nBuyers should verify the RERA registration certificate, approved building plans, land ownership documents, commencement certificate, construction schedule, and draft agreement for sale. It is strongly recommended to have a property lawyer review all documents before paying a booking amount or signing any agreement.\n\n### Are there near-possession or almost ready new projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nYes, some new projects in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** may be close to completion and offer possession within a short timeframe. These are often referred to as near-possession projects. Buyers should confirm the expected occupancy certificate date, availability of basic utilities, and final handover conditions before proceeding.\n\n### What additional costs should I budget for when buying a new project flat in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nBeyond the base price, buyers should account for GST (if applicable), stamp duty, registration charges, legal fees, maintenance deposits, corpus fund contributions, parking charges (if applicable), and interior fit-out expenses. Understanding the full cost structure helps avoid last-minute financial pressure.\n\n### How does Houssed help buyers choose the right new project in Malabar Hill, Mumbai?\n\nHoussed operates as a **decision-support platform**, offering verified listings of new projects in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** with clear possession status, regulatory indicators, and structured comparisons. Buyers can evaluate under-construction flats across budgets, BHK configurations, and project stages without relying on promotional claims, enabling more informed and lower-risk decisions.\n\n## New Projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai - Under-Construction Flats & Residential Developments\n\n### Overview of New Residential Projects in Malabar Hill, Mumbai\n\nNew projects in **Malabar Hill, Mumbai** refer to under-construction and newly launched residential developments offering flats with future possession timelines. These projects att